From a7f60b593a73a52e79ba59fd7ba907b7bd9015bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:32:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): "Take over here" on a chat open in another
 Hermes window [daveey]

The SESSION_NOT_OWNED error card now offers "Take over here" before
"Start new chat": it calls session.take_over for this chat's live runtime
(routed to the owning profile through the session-tile delegate), warns
when the other window did not confirm in time, refreshes the transcript
from the store, then re-runs the refused prompt via message().reload()
(the Retry path). Failures surface through notifyError.

- error-surface.ts: ErrorRecoveryPlan.takeOver (SESSION_NOT_OWNED only).
- status.ts: the gateway `error` event's own error_surface wins over text
  sniffing (the takeover watcher sends SESSION_NOT_OWNED).
- i18n: errorTakeOver / errorTakeOverUnconfirmed / errorTakeOverFailed in
  en/de/es/fr/ja/zh/zh-hant/ar (ru listed in overlay-gaps like its
  siblings); SESSION_NOT_OWNED body points at taking it over.
- Retry/limit-reset buttons moved into RetryActions (keeps the card's
  complexity under its cap).
